        <title>WritePolicyBench: Benchmarking Memory Write Policies under Byte Budgets</title>
        <authors>Edgard El Cham</authors>
        <categories>cs.PF</categories>
            <comments>10 pages, 4 figures</comments>
            <license>http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</license>
            <abstract>We introduce WritePolicyBench, a benchmark for evaluating memory write policies: decision rules that choose what to store, merge, and evict under a strict byte budget while processing a stream with document/API drift. The benchmark provides (i) task generators with controlled non-stationarity, (ii) an explicit action interface for external memory, (iii) a byte-accurate cost model, and (iv) standardized metrics that measure both task success and budget efficiency.</abstract>
